Subject: Subsetting character by names
Message-ID: <ekfxGCnkiRc.D9pQvhViEAAJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/israel-r-user-group/c/ekfxGCnkiRc/m/D9pQvhViEAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Suppose I have
mySillyQuestion<-c("avner", "moshe", "haim", "moti", "tal", "amit")

I want to get all the names between moshe and tal without using index.

I tried subset(mySillyQuestion, select = moshe:tal)

What is the easiet way to do it? (the hard way is to use dplyr and select() columns after reshape)

Thanks,

Avner

From uc0e822e430c1a5a7 at groups.google.com  Sun Aug  7 09:41:03 2016
From: uc0e822e430c1a5a7 at groups.google.com (Michael Dorman)
